[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every report about wrong dates into one ticket, because their
subject lines matched ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Read by what each
report describes, the ticket holds three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but only two of its three problems are dealt with. The one-day shift has no fix.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {repo} {rows} />

## How the reports were split

- **One report, one count.** The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice. Counted by id.
- **Cause by tenant, not by intake tag.** Intake guesses `parser` or `hint` from the reporter's
  browser. The cause depends on the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`).
- **A one-day move is not a swap.** The desk read some reports as a one-day move
  (`desk-notes.json`) but filed them under `parser` by tenant. A swapped day and month moves a
  booking by months. These moved it by one day, differently for clients in different time zones,
  and in one case only in June. The parser fix does not reach them.

## What to watch

- The parser fix covers "eu locales". Harbour Dental writes `en-GB`, which is not an EU locale:
  check that its reports stop.
- A new one-day report belongs to the day-shift ticket, not to #4471.

